===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰel-|id=blow}}
From {{inh|en|enm|bal}}, {{m|enm|ball}}, {{m|enm|balle}}, from an unattested {{inh|en|ang|*beall}}, {{m|ang|*bealla||round object, ball}} or {{der|en|non|bǫllr||a ball}}, both from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*balluz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*ballô||ball}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰoln-||bubble}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰel-||to blow, inflate, swell|id=blow}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|ball}}, {{cog|nl|bal}}, {{cog|goh|bal}}, {{m|goh|ballo}} ({{cog|de|Ball||ball}}; {{m|de|Ballen||bale}}). Related forms in Romance are borrowings from Germanic. See also {{l|en|balloon}}, {{l|en|bale}}.
[[Image:Basketball.jpeg|thumb|A basketball]]

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# A solid or hollow [[sphere]], or roughly spherical mass.
#: {{ux|en|a '''ball''' of spittle; a fecal '''ball'''}}
## A quantity of string, thread, etc., wound into a spherical shape.
##: {{ux|en|a '''ball''' of wool; a '''ball''' of twine}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} Homologue or analogue of a [[disk]] in the [[Euclidean plane]].
## {{lb|en|mathematics}} In 3-dimensional Euclidean space, the volume bounded by a [[sphere]].
## {{lb|en|mathematics}} The set of points in a [[metric space]] of any number of [[dimension]]s lying within a given distance (the [[radius]]) of a given point.
## {{lb|en|mathematics}} The set of points in a [[topological space]] lying within some [[open set]] containing a given point.
# {{lb|en|ballistics|firearms}} A solid, spherical nonexplosive missile for a cannon, rifle, gun, etc.
## A [[jacket]]ed non-[[expand]]ing bullet, typically of [[military]] origin.
## {{lb|en|uncountable|obsolete}} Such bullets collectively.
##* {{quote-text|en|year=1659|author=w:Arthur Annesley, 1st Earl of Anglesey|title=England’s Confusion|url=http://name.umdl.umich.edu/A69468.0001.001|page=7|location=London
|passage={{...}} the ''Good Old Cause'', which, as they seemed to represent it, smelt of Gunpowder and '''ball''' {{...}}}}
##* {{RQ:Defoe Robinson Crusoe|page=294|text=I gave each of them a Musket with a Firelock on it, and about eight Charges of Powder and '''Ball''', charging them to be very good Husbands of both, and not to use either of them but upon urgent Occasion.}}
##* {{quote-text|en|year=1803|author=w:Robert Charles Dallas|title=The History of the Maroons|location=London|publisher=Longman and Rees|section=Volume 1, Letter 5, p. 148|url=https://archive.org/details/cihm_44228
|passage={{...}} some headstrong Maroons were using a soldier of Captain Craskell’s ill, and compelling him to write to his commander, that it was too late to do any thing good, and that they wanted nothing, having got plenty of powder and '''ball''' {{...}}}}
##* {{RQ:Melville Moby-Dick|chapter=1|page=1|passage=This is my substitute for pistol and '''ball'''. With a philosophical flourish Cato throws himself upon his sword; I quietly take to the ship.}}
# A roundish, [[protuberant]] portion of some part of the body.
#: {{ux|en|the '''ball''' of the thumb}}
## {{lb|en|anatomy}} The front of the bottom of the [[foot]], just behind the toes.
# The [[globe]]; the earthly sphere.
#* ''c. 1712''', {{w|Joseph Addison}}, ''[[s:Hymns for the Amusement of Children (1791)/Ode to the Creator|Ode to the Creator of the World]]''
#*: What, though in solemn Silence, all / Move round the dark terrestrial '''Ball'''!
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1717|author=w:Alexander Pope|title=s:Elegy to the Memory of an Unfortunate Lady
|passage=Thus, if eternal Justice rules the '''ball''', / Thus shall your wives, and thus your children fall;}}
# {{lb|en|sports|countable}} An object that is the focus of many sports and games, in which it may be thrown, caught, kicked, bounced, rolled, chased, retrieved, hit with an instrument, spun, etc., usually roughly spherical but whose size, weight,   bounciness, colour, etc. differ according to the game
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1922|author=w:Michael Arlen| title=[http://openlibrary.org/works/OL1519647W “Piracy”: A Romantic Chronicle of These Days]| chapter=3/19/2| passage=Ivor had acquired more than a mile of fishing rights with the house; he was not at all a good fisherman, but one must do something; one generally, however, banged a '''ball''' with a squash-racket against a wall.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=October 2, 2011|author=Aled Williams|work=BBC Sport Wales
|title=[http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/eng_prem/15051279.stm Swansea 2-0 Stoke]
|passage=Graham secured victory with five minutes left, coolly lifting the '''ball''' over Asmir Begovic.}}
## {{label|en|uncountable}} Any sport or game involving a ball; its play, literally or figuratively.
##: {{ux|en|The children were playing '''ball''' on the beach.}} {{ux|en|George played his college '''ball''' at Stanford.}}
## {{senseid|en|baseball}}{{lb|en|baseball|countable}} A [[pitch]] that falls outside of the [[strike zone]].
## {{lb|en|pinball|countable}} An opportunity to launch the [[pinball]] into play.
##: {{ux|en|If you get to a million points, you get another '''ball'''.}}
## {{lb|en|cricket|countable}} A single [[delivery]] by the [[bowler]], six of which make up an [[over]].
## {{lb|en|soccer|countable}} A [[pass]]; a kick of the [[football]] towards a teammate.
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=December 29, 2010|author=Chris Whyatt|work=BBC
|title=[http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/eng_prem/9309542.stm Chelsea 1-0 Bolton]
|passage=After Essien's poor attempt flew into the stands, Rodrigo Moreno—Bolton's on-loan winger from Benfica who was making his full Premier League debut—nearly exposed the Blues with a lovely '''ball''' for Johan Elmander, but it just skipped away from his team-mate's toes.}}
# {{lb|en|mildly|vulgar|slang|usually|in the plural}} A [[testicle]].
## {{lb|en|in the plural}} [[nonsense|Nonsense]].
##: {{ux|en|That’s a load of '''balls''', and you know it!}}
## {{lb|en|in the plural}} [[courage|Courage]].
##: {{ux|en|I doubt he’s got the '''balls''' to tell you off.}}
# {{lb|en|printing|historical}} A leather-covered cushion, fastened to a handle called a [[ballstock]]; formerly used by printers for inking the form, then superseded by the [[roller]].
# {{lb|en|farriery|historical}} A large [[pill]], a form in which [[medicine]] was given to horses; a [[bolus]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1842|author=James White|title=A compendium of the veterinary art
|passage=The ''laxative alterative'' has not this advantage, the aloes, of which it is composed, being extremely bitter, and therefore requiring to be given in the form of a '''''ball'''''.}}
# {{lb|en|slang|countable|uncountable|singular only}} One thousand [[US dollar]]s.
#* {{quote-song|en|date=22-07-2022|lyricist=w:YoungBoy Never Broke Again|url=https://genius.com/Youngboy-never-broke-again-convict-life-wanna-be-alone-lyrics|title=Convict Life (Wanna Be Alone)|passage=I'ma let these niggas have it, go on stage and throw a forty '''ball'''}}
#* {{quote-song|en|date=16-09-2022|lyricist=Su'Lan|title=Hands on the Floor|url=https://genius.com/Sulan-hands-on-the-floor-lyrics|album=Forever Da Gang|track=4|time=[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CqcC5gLBx4Y&t=40 0:40]|passage=Forty '''ball''' all in these leather jeans<br/>Diamonds studs, I make a bum nigga think twice}}
#* {{quote-song|en|date=23-11-2022|lyricist=GoldenBoy Countup|title=10PM in ATL|url=https://genius.com/Goldenboy-countup-10pm-in-atl-lyrics|album=Chill|track=2|passage=Forty '''ball''' on my wrist, nigga, I cashed out on it (Damn)<br/>Forty bands on my neck, nigga, I maxed out on it (Damn)}}
